---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Arrow from '../components/Arrow.astro';
---
<Base
  title="About | Hasan Shahriar"
  description="Hasan Shahriar is a product builder and founder in Helsinki, by way of Bangladesh."
  pageSchemaType="ProfilePage"
>
  <header class="page-hero about-hero shell">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1>I was building long before I knew “builder” was a career.</h1>
  </header>

  <section class="about-intro shell">
    <div class="portrait-placeholder" aria-label="Portrait coming soon">
      <span>Portrait<br/>coming later</span>
      <i>Dhaka ↗ Helsinki</i>
    </div>
    <div class="about-intro__copy">
      <p class="large-copy">I’m Hasan—a founder and product builder in Helsinki, by way of Bangladesh.</p>
      <p>My uncle never wrote a business plan. He saw a thing he wanted, pulled in people he liked, and moved. As a kid I watched that work, and copied it without knowing I was copying anything.</p>
      <p>Then I became an immigrant and picked up a second voice: the one that asks <em>lokey ki bolbe</em>—what will people say—before doing anything. A lot of my work and writing is the practice of taking the chair back from that voice.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--ink">
    <div class="shell about-now">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Now</p>
        <h2>I build across product, engineering and the business around them.</h2>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p>At Zipli, I lead product and engineering for an AI-assisted food-surplus platform. Through Makeshift, I have worked with founders, agencies and enterprise teams across direct and partner engagements.</p>
        <p>Most of my time goes to Zipli. The rest goes to writing, which is how I find out what I actually think.</p>
        <a class="button button--light" href="mailto:hasan@hasanshahriar.com">Say hello <Arrow /></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section shell principles">
    <p class="eyebrow">A few operating beliefs</p>
    <div class="principle-grid">
      <div><span>01</span><h3>Sent, not saved.</h3><p>The only useful information arrives after the work meets the world.</p></div>
      <div><span>02</span><h3>People are infrastructure.</h3><p>The teams that survive the difficult middle are rarely assembled by résumé alone.</p></div>
      <div><span>03</span><h3>Closeness is a moat.</h3><p>When building gets cheap, understanding the real operating context becomes more valuable.</p></div>
      <div><span>04</span><h3>Humour is the way.</h3><p>If the explanation cannot breathe, the thinking probably cannot either.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
